// WIRED 17 August 2026, task #116, Phase C.
//
// ── THE WARNING HAS TO COME BEFORE THE TAP, NOT AFTER ────────────────────
//
// amendStayBooking sends a booking BACK TO PENDING when the dates change on a
// request-mode listing. The host agreed to particular nights; moving them
// without asking would let a guest turn an accepted weekend into a fortnight.
//
// That is standard on every comparable platform, and it is also the one place
// in this whole feature where using a screen can leave a guest LESS certain
// than they were before they touched it — a confirmed stay becomes a request
// again. So it is stated on this screen, before Confirm, whenever the change
// would actually cause it. Reporting it afterwards would be telling somebody
// what you have done to their holiday.
//
// A party-size change does not do this, and the warning correctly stays hidden
// for it.
//
// ── THE PRICE COMES FROM THE SERVER, ALWAYS ──────────────────────────────
//
// Every edit re-quotes through quoteStayAmendment. The screen never multiplies
// a nightly rate by a night count to show a total — that is how the displayed
// figure and the charged figure drift apart.
